# Phone-side registry mirrors -- TEMPLATE, safe to commit.
#
# The agent has NO compiled-in mirror hosts. Configure them per device:
#   env vars (set by whoever launches the agent), or
#   $DROIDNODE_DATA_DIR/registry-mirrors.env   (this file's copy)
# Env wins over the file. Empty or missing = pull the upstream directly.
#
# The real file is runtime configuration, not source: keep it out of git.
# deploy/registry-mirrors.env is gitignored.
#
# Keys (same names the agent reads):
#   DROIDNODE_REGISTRY_MIRROR       docker.io / registry-1.docker.io / index.docker.io
#   DROIDNODE_REGISTRY_MIRROR_K8S   registry.k8s.io
#   DROIDNODE_REGISTRY_MIRROR_QUAY  quay.io
#
# Push to a debug build and restart the agent:
#   adb push deploy\registry-mirrors.env /data/local/tmp/
#   adb shell "cat /data/local/tmp/registry-mirrors.env | run-as com.droidnode sh -c 'cat > files/registry-mirrors.env'"
#   # then Settings -> 重启, or force-stop and reopen the app
#
# Or skip adb entirely: edit the same three values in the app under
# Settings -> 节点 -> 镜像源. Saving writes this exact file and restarts the agent;
# the row underneath shows what the agent reports as in effect.
#
# DROIDNODE_REGISTRY_MIRROR=<your-docker-mirror-host>
# DROIDNODE_REGISTRY_MIRROR_K8S=<your-k8s-mirror-host>
# DROIDNODE_REGISTRY_MIRROR_QUAY=<your-quay-mirror-host>
